  "_comment": [
    "Loader layouts and download locations. Fetched at runtime by the Manager so that a",
    "layout change on BepInEx's or MelonLoader's side is fixed by editing this file, without",
    "publishing a new binary. See analyse/loader-catalog-dynamic.md.",
    "",
    "'sources' (schema 5) is what makes versions stop being maintained by hand. Each entry says",
    "WHERE to look and WHICH assets are ours; the Manager reads the list the publisher actually",
    "put out and filters it. It never composes a file name: composing means knowing every case in",
    "advance, so the day BepInEx ships a win-arm64 build a reader sees it and a template does not.",
    "The three projects name their files three different ways, and each list also contains things",
    "that are NOT loaders — BepInEx_Patcher_*, BepInEx's NET.CoreCLR/NET.Framework builds,",
    "MelonLoader.Installer.*. A prefix that matches nothing is simply skipped.",
    "",
    "'version', 'github' and 'assets' STAY, and must never be removed. Nothing verifies 'schema'",
    "— no code reads it — so a Manager already installed cannot refuse a file it does not",
    "understand: it would ignore the new fields in silence and install nothing. They are the",
    "pinned fallback: what older binaries use, what an offline install uses, and where resolution",
    "lands when a source cannot be reached.",
    "",
    "BepInEx 6 carries two sources because it has no stable release at all — its GitHub page",
    "stopped at a pre-release in August 2024 while development continued in Bleeding Edge builds.",
    "Which one is used is a Manager setting (bepinex6_channel), not a per-game choice.",
    "",
    "Checksums are NOT listed here. Neither project publishes .sha256 files, but GitHub exposes",
    "a sha256 digest for every release asset through its API, and the Manager reads it there.",
    "Pinning a hash in this file stays possible (asset.sha256) and takes precedence — use it only",
    "when a specific file must be guaranteed, because a pinned hash goes stale on every version",
    "bump and a stale hash blocks installs for everyone.",
    "⚠ BepInEx 6 has no digest in EITHER channel: the 2024 release predates the feature and the",
    "build server publishes none. HTTPS is all there is there, and the tool says so.",
    "",
        "Each warning carries the situation it applies to (os / runtimes / on_fresh_install). A note",
    "shown when it is not true teaches the reader to skip warnings, which is the one habit they",
    "must not have. Facts about platforms we do not offer belong in this comment, not on screen."
  ],

